course: dictionary
lesson: 5080
title: Insulin, the body's sugar key
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your body runs on sugar from food, but sugar cannot get into your cells on its own. Insulin is a hormone, which is a chemical messenger in the blood, and it works like a key that lets the sugar in.
explain: Insulin is made by the pancreas, an organ behind the stomach. The example «In type 1 diabetes the immune system has destroyed the insulin-making cells of the pancreas» shows what happens when those cells are damaged: the body cannot make enough insulin.
explain: Insulin is also a medicine. The example «A hypo is blood sugar too low, from too much insulin, too little food or extra exercise» shows that the sugar in your blood can drop too far, and this is why people with diabetes must check it carefully.
fact: Insulin is a hormone, a chemical messenger in the blood.
fact: Insulin lets sugar from food into your cells, where it is used for energy.
fact: The pancreas is an organ behind the stomach that makes insulin.
fact: A «hypo» is blood sugar that is too low, and its signs include shaking, sweating, paleness and confusion.
fact: Insulin is uncountable, so we say «some insulin», not «an insulin».
exercise: In the sentence «insulin lets sugar from food into cells for energy», what job does insulin do? | Stores air in the blood | *Lets sugar from food into the cells for energy | Turns water into sugar | Makes the food taste sweeter
exercise: Which organ makes insulin? | *The pancreas | The brain | The heart | The lungs
exercise: Which is a sign of a hypo? | Eating extra vegetables | Growing taller | *Shaking and sweating | Singing loudly
test: Insulin is a hormone that helps the body use sugar from food. What is a hormone? | A type of food | A kind of bone | A part of the stomach | *A chemical messenger in the blood
test: «Children with type 1 diabetes can eat most foods if they count the carbohydrates.» What are carbs? | Muscles | Vitamins | *The sugar and starch in food | Water
exam: Which sentence uses insulin correctly? | Insulin is an insulin for the pancreas | *Some insulin is needed to let sugar into the cells | Insulin is a food that you eat with bread | The insulin lives in the lungs
